From e7f7e6fe8dfcaa244f2c15b628083a740d23fe51 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sun, 22 Nov 2026 08:32:38 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Air battle sound: the close view's guns stand out of the
 ridden engine; a twin mount is one take

From the Bremen r2d film (22 Nov, 0001-0018), measured and re-checked:
- The chase view came out louder (-13.7 LUFS, was -16.4) but not more intense:
  the quiet between attacks rose 4.4 dB and the bursts did not, so the bursts
  stood 5.1 LU over the bed instead of 9.4. Every burst already reaches the
  limiter's ceiling; the ridden engine is 70% of the sound between attacks.
  mix.json: air.closeView.masterDb 7.5 -> 9.5 and bed.gainDb 6 -> 1 (the
  engine 3 dB under the film, everything else 2 dB over). Re-mixed from the
  film through the game's limiter: chase -14.1 LUFS, bursts 7.2 LU over the
  bed, limiter more than 0.5 dB down 3.5% of the time.
- A 10 s wall at 116-127 s was a B-17 box's gunners firing at the ridden
  Fw 190. A twin mount laid two identical takes on the same frame (+6 dB,
  in step). AirBattle.cpp: a gunner's mount (guns of one aircraft, kind and
  mount within a metre this frame) is now heard as one take at the square
  root of its guns, as a fighter's wing already is; its take stops with the
  last of its guns (WingOf/WingLive).
- Notes corrected where the code differs: no +12 dB per-sound limit bites
  (_masterDb), masterDbByCameraDistance measures to the nearest group, and
  closeView._notBuilt lists the keys no code reads.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01L4rhz35oCkUv94Xb2EwCjp
